    {
      "week": 38,
      "slug": "seams-and-cuts",
      "title": "Seams and cuts",
      "idea": "A joined strip's seam controls its boundary circles, connected pieces after a center cut, and transported arrow direction.",
      "gates": "K-1 is conditional on reliably tracing through a real seam with adult support. Grades 2-3 track upper/lower seam connections. Grades 4-5 separate piece and boundary counts and explain arrow reversal. Count to four; adults may read.",
      "materials": "Marked paper strips, tape, removable dots and transverse arrows, washable markers and adult scissors. Build the exact matching-order and reversed-order seams; all cutting is adult-only.",
      "pretest": "Mandatory exact-material tests remain unperformed: trace boundaries, make complete center cuts, check piece/edge counts, and test continuous arrow transport. Keep loops on the table and away from bodies.",
