    {
      "week": 39,
      "slug": "road-detours",
      "title": "Road detours",
      "idea": "Canceling immediate road reversals gives a unique reduced journey; a tree, one ring and two rings reveal what order can preserve.",
      "gates": "K-1 must replay an ordered route and remove an immediate reversal without reordering the rest. Grades 2-3 compare tree and ring results. Grades 4-5 explain unique reduction and the zero-net-count obstruction. Counting to 12 helps; adults may record.",
      "materials": "Pawns, fixed road mats, large directed-step tiles with road identities, erasable pens and adult recording. The roads stay in place when recorded journey steps are removed.",
      "pretest": "The exact tiles, mats and recording workflow remain untested. Rehearse the printed four-step example and its shortened replay. Stay with short adult-recorded routes if ordering is not reliable.",
