    {
      "week": 40,
      "slug": "loop-color-certificates",
      "title": "Loop color certificates",
      "idea": "Whole-arc colorings distinguish a trefoil from a plain loop, with local checks and an explicitly supplied global invariant theorem.",
      "gates": "K-1 is optional and conditional: distinguish over/under and trace a complete unworked target arc before coloring. Grades 2-3 count colorings and test unique local completion. Grades 4-5 use the invariant and its one-way limitation.",
      "materials": "Checked closed-cord models on trays, full-size 148 mm diagrams, tracing paper and three labeled marker colors. Preserve underpass gaps; children never cut or wear loops.",
      "pretest": "Mandatory cord-model, marker-channel and handling tests are unperformed. Verify every crossing and closure in the trefoil and reverse the construction of the complicated unknots. If arc transfer fails, defer coloring tasks.",
