    {
      "week": 41,
      "slug": "torus-portals",
      "title": "Torus portals and lifts",
      "idea": "A portal route lifts to a repeated map; its finishing copy records winding and determines whether a whole loop can contract.",
      "gates": "K-1 must cross a seam without reversing direction or changing row/column. Grades 2-3 distinguish home from the original home copy. Grades 4-5 connect winding to square slides and backtracks. Adults may read arrows and record.",
      "materials": "Full-size 180 mm portal mats, pawns, tracing paper, and separate 90 mm table copies with spare extensions. Compact recording arrays need pencil traces or enlarged working mats.",
      "pretest": "Exact mats, copies, extensions and pawn/tracing handling remain untested. Check matching opposite-edge marks without reversal, add copies before reaching the edge, and test the two-pawn task. Trimming is adult-only.",
